# GT4: TIMED arm B of the paired ABAB (audits off): A = c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace (control), B = c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace-pairslice; the pair differs in QWEN_FAST_GDN_PAIR_SLICE alone (the tp4-gluefix-jobs arms).
# These profiles keep the V2 glue OFF, so the flag is the live path in B: a real gain here is what the pair slice is for (the best-ship profiles keep V2 on, where the flag is idle by construction, and are not timed).
# Arms alternate A B A B, each after its own all-four reset, same admission order. Runs only if G1 passed (NEEDS in ORDER.txt).
# READ: the '[PACKED-PHASE]' and round lines of the four-user tests judged PAIRED per round (never by unpaired medians), the GDN slice time in the phase lines, and offline the SMOKE_JSON results compared test by test
# and user by user (content_sha256, reasoning_sha256, completion_tokens, finish identical A against B). Check the load average; no CI pushes while a timed arm runs. Duration (estimate): 55 min. Soft.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/next-5 four-card development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/next-5 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-5a is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/next-5 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next-5a
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-speed-strace-pairslice
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4_code_equal,concurrent4_code_32k
